Test the UPF201 pseudopotential reader with no cutoff_radius_index and a
multi-line PP_LOCAL header. Symmetry remains enabled.

Reference validation (2026-10-28)
--------------------------------
The former input retained 10 bands for 17 electrons. Its highest band was
still partially occupied, and CG and PPCG reached different self-consistent
states: -2225.032737484868 and -2364.170263765835 eV, respectively. Both met
the original SCF stopping criterion. Tightening scf_thr to 1e-11 and allowing
200 diagonalization iterations while keeping 10 bands did not remove this
disagreement: CG remained at -2225.032737542274 eV, while Davidson and PPCG
reached approximately -2364.17026379 eV.

The revised input retains 20 bands, uses scf_thr=1e-11, and permits 200
diagonalization iterations. The structure, pseudopotential, plane-wave
cutoff, electron count, symmetry, smearing, and default CG solver are
unchanged. The additional bands are unoccupied at convergence. Increasing
the retained space again to 24 bands confirms stability of the energy.

Independent solver results using the revised precision:

  Bands   CG energy (eV)       Davidson energy (eV)  PPCG energy (eV)
  20      -2364.170263789949   -2364.170263789398    -2364.170263789641
  24      -2364.170263790098   -2364.170263790731    -2364.170263791520

All six runs converged. Their energy span is 2.122e-9 eV, below the existing
1e-7 eV tolerance. Keeping the original SCF precision with 20 bands gave a
CG/Davidson difference of 1.985e-7 eV; the revised precision settings bring
the solver comparison within the original tolerance.

The stored energy reference comes from the independent 20-band CG run.
The other reference properties and all acceptance tolerances are unchanged.
With this reference, CG, Davidson, and PPCG were each run at 1, 2, and 4 MPI
ranks: all nine official Autotest runs passed all five checked properties.
All nine SCF runs converged, their energy span was 2.716e-9 eV, and there
were no PPCG residual warnings.

Validation used GNU 12.3, OpenMPI 5.0.10, CPU Release, and one thread each
for OpenMP, OpenBLAS, and MKL. The executable was built from base commit
77f7b4af69934064aa5f4b84267343e9135bc348 plus the locally validated solver
changes; its SHA-256 is
7f14de6005560b6df11b7cf968a47ee52eb5fc4a379e5de7acec43228a114cac.
The unchanged original input and reference remain in that base commit.

To reproduce, use clean copies of this case with ks_solver=cg, dav, and
ppcg and run the unchanged tests/integrate/Autotest.sh at -n1, -n2, and
-n4 with -o1. Also compare the three solvers at nbands=24. Do not reuse
wavefunctions, densities, or other outputs between solver runs.
